course: dictionary
lesson: 13770
title: Getting involved
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To intervene means to get involved in a situation to stop it or change it, especially to help. «The teacher intervened when two boys started to shove each other.» The teacher stepped in, so the pushing stopped. Look for clues: who acted, and what changed because of it.
explain: Intervene has a second meaning: to come between two times or events. «In the intervening years, the village built a new school.» The intervening years are the years that came between two other times. You can often spot this meaning when the sentence talks about time, like «the intervening weeks».
explain: Intervene is often followed by «in», as in «intervene in a fight». Be careful: stepping in is not always safe. «If you see someone being picked on, you can intervene safely by fetching an adult.» Getting help from a grown-up is often the safest way to help.
fact: To intervene means to get involved to stop a situation or change it.
fact: «Intervene» can also mean to come between two times or events.
fact: «The intervening time» means the time that comes between two events.
fact: «Intervene in» means to get involved in something, as in «intervene in a fight».
fact: The safest way to help in a dangerous situation is often to fetch an adult.
exercise: «The teacher intervened when the argument got loud.» What does intervened mean? | Joined in the shouting | Went home early | Ran out of the room | *Got involved to stop it
exercise: «In the intervening years, the school was painted twice.» What does intervening mean here? | Very loud | The best years | *Between the two times | The final years
exercise: Maya sees a bully and wants to help. What is the safest way to intervene? | Film it on a phone | Stand between them alone and shout | Join in with the bully | *Fetch an adult to help
test: «The referee intervened when a player was hurt.» What does intervened mean? | Left the field | Ignored the game | *Got involved to stop or change what was happening | Stopped the clock forever
test: «Many things changed in the intervening time.» What does intervening time mean? | Future time | The time after everything ended | *The time that came between two events | The time before anything started
exam: «The government intervened to help the flood victims.» What is the best meaning of intervened? | Ran away from the flood | Watched quietly from far away | Built a wall for fun | *Got involved to help and change the situation
